  "query_preview": "..\nSynoptic Setup: A cold front is dropping south across Montana \nthis afternoon. Quite a difference in conditions north of the \nfront this afternoon with clouds, scattered showers and temps in \nthe 50s over the northern zones with 60s and 70s to the south with\nmore sunshine.\n\nModels did not pick up today's precipitation very well. The\nstrength of the jet stream could have been the culprit and\nsometimes models struggle with shoulder season (Spring and Fall)\nevents.\n\nTonight, clearing is expected with surface high pressure dropping\nin from the Canadian prairies. There could be enough radiational\ncooling that sends temps to near freezing in a few locations. But\nmidlevel clouds late could save some locations.\n\nA subtle shortwave at the mid levels is expected to move through \nthe southern zones early Thursday and kick off a few stratiform \nshowers. Temps will be quite cool Thursday with surface high \npressure in place and should be the coolest day in this forecast \nperiod. Frost has the potential again for Thursday night and\nFriday but it looks like clouds could keep temps from plummeting.\n\nSaturday into Monday: Surface high pressure over the Canadian \nprairies looks to be in place this weekend with flow becoming full\nNW. This will keep daytime temps near normal with dry conditions.\n\nMonday night onward: Ensembles show a ridge building into the area\nfor dry conditions and above normal temps.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nDeviations to NBM:\n\n- Lowered temps tonight toward NBM10.\n\nMany changes were made this morning to mainly raise pops and lower\ntemps. TFJ",
